      "message": "A few more comments after reading the DP alt mode spec:\n* The PD spec and DP alt mode 2.1 spec seem to agree that VDM version 2.1 means PD r3.1 v1.6 or newer. They imply that all VDMs sent by a port should have the same VDM version. I think I\u0027m missing something here. Why have VDM versions if 1) they are not specific to types of VDMs and 2) they are redundant with the PD revision?\n* It seems like this is intended to be used to set our own VDM version going out. If that\u0027s the case, it seems like it should also consider the VDM version we got from the partner. PD r 3.1 v 1.8 ss 6.4.4.2.3: \"After discovering the Structure VDM Version, the Structured VDM Version field Shall match the agreed common Structured VDM Version.\"\n* Whatever this is for, it seems like it should have a much more specific name than it has now.",
