      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-07T23:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems an interface that will be easy to use correctly, since the caller has to remember the format of this bespoke bit field. I might be OK with a function with 3 `bool` output parameters, but that also seems a bit clunky. I\u0027d rather have 3 functions that each returned `bool`.\n\nI don\u0027t see the caller even using the retimer/redriver bit. Does that need to be there?\n\nI haven\u0027t grokked the implementation yet, but it seems like a lot to take in. To my mind, that would also argue for separate functions.",
      "revId": "cbe321c1502d127cb9060bbdb9bb8979bef15d08",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "909ae7da_c1b2934a",
        "filename": "include/usb_pd_dp.h",
        "patchSetId": 38
      },
      "lineNbr": 148,
      "author": {
        "id": 1131142
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-20T22:55:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked into the implementation and to me it makes sense to keep it as a bitfield since it is polling both the dp and tbt vdo messages to create a response of the supported cable type. I prefer to not split this out as that means more calls to those vdo messages to get the same information that we could have just gotten all at once.\n\nIt does look like retimer/redriver bit is not used right now but that doesn\u0027t mean there won\u0027t be a reason it is needed later",
      "parentUuid": "58855345_022fcab6",
      "revId": "cbe321c1502d127cb9060bbdb9bb8979bef15d08",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
